scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: firefly
run_id: 3
total_caught: 1
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 5
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 13.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed distinguishing NotFound from parse/permission errors
    in from_file_or_default. Dev summary mentions 'TOML loading' but no evidence of
    error-type discrimination.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA explicitly listed 'CWE-209 error exposure' and 'error message length
    bounds' as security tests in exit_codes.rs (11 tests covering AC-3 exit codes
    and CWE-209 error info leakage).
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA tested header injection (CRLF in tenant) and dev implemented 'header\
    \ injection prevention', which mitigates the injection vector at runtime. However,\
    \ the core finding is that SiemClient.tenant_id is a raw String bypassing the\
    \ type-safe TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 no phase flagged the type mismatch\
    \ or recommended using Option<TenantId>."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev Cargo.toml changes show 'added chrono and uuid deps' with direct versions.
    No phase flagged the 6 dependencies using direct version strings instead of workspace
    = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'TEA tested ''token-not-in-file security'' which is about not storing
    tokens, not about detecting unknown fields. No phase flagged missing #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]
    or the risk of silently ignored config keys.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: This is a bug in the pipeline's own test output. The vacuously true assertion
    (is_none() || ...) was not caught by the reviewer phase, which produced no output.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: This is a bug in the pipeline's own test output. The zero-assertion test
    (let _ = config) was not caught by the reviewer phase, which produced no output.
